--- a/PEOPLE_DATE_AUDIT.md
+++ b/PEOPLE_DATE_AUDIT.md
@@ -338,3 +338,29 @@ Retrospective is the sole later-reception category, including commemorations and
 references after a known death. Use kind `retrospective-reference` or, on a narrower
 honor/work claim, receptionType `retrospective`. Do not require proof of death,
 introduce a posthumous subtype, or change the separate `posthumous-name` alias kind.
+# Explicit evidence holds
+
+`data/people/date-audit-holds.json` is a mandatory tracked manifest. Its empty
+`holds` array means no explicit holds; a missing or malformed manifest is an
+error, never an empty manifest. The root-level people data file is included in
+the existing sparse-checkout patterns. Each active entry has `status: "active"`,
+`book`, three-digit `chapter`, `auditVersion`, `reportFileHash`, `sourceHash`,
+`extractionHash`, substantive `reason`, `reportedBy`, `createdAt`, and a nonempty
+`evidence` array of `{path, sha256}`. Hashes use the `sha256:` prefix. The report
+hash pins exact UTF-8 report file bytes; source and extraction hashes are the
+original audit report's packet fingerprints. Evidence paths are repository-relative
+and their hashes pin the independently reviewed evidence files. Confirm these pins
+before adding a record; a syntactically valid hash alone does not prove a finding.
+
+An entry keeps its chapter `research-blocked` even when reports, source or
+extraction later change or disappear. The original report and queue state are not
+changed. Do not remove a hold merely because a fingerprint changed or a new report
+exists. No crash-safe hold-resolution mechanism is implemented yet: removing an
+entry while the old report remains installed could silently revive that approval.
+Hold removal is prohibited until a separate reviewed resolution protocol exists.
+Automatic date workflows and report recording refuse held chapters. These checks
+are not a cross-process lock: simultaneous hold installation and publication need
+host coordination and may race between checks.
+Rebuild the catalog, site index and progress after hold changes so cached status
+and displayed metrics reflect them; ebook validation also checks current status.
+
